{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having abdominal pain. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started two days ago—just a dull ache at first, but it got worse yesterday. Now it's sharp in the middle and upper part of my belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any nausea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:18:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I threw up once this morning. It was dark, but I don’t think it was blood. I haven’t eaten anything since the pain started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Your history shows you’ve had similar pain before and a few G-tube placements. Are you still on tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I’m off the 24-hour feeds now. I’ve been on a bariatric stage 3 diet—soft foods. But I stopped everything when the pain came on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now. We’ll start IV fluids and manage your pain. We also need to check your G-tube site and get a CT scan to see what’s going on near the surgical area."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:22:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will the pain get worse? I’m worried it’s another leak or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching for that. The CT will help us rule out a leak. For now, we’ll give you IV pain meds and keep your G-tube to gravity drainage—that often helps relieve pressure and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-07-03 22:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-07-04 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your CT results back. There’s significant inflammation near the spot where your stomach was reconnected after the bypass reversal. No clear leak, but we can’t rule out a tiny one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-07-04 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it infected? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-07-04 19:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks like inflammation, possibly from irritation or early infection. We’re starting you on antibiotics—ciprofloxacin and metronidazole—to cover any possible infection. We’ll keep you NPO a bit longer and monitor your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-07-04 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be on IV meds the whole time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-07-04 19:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. But if you improve, we’ll switch to oral meds and slowly restart your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-07-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-07-05 08:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, actually. Still some discomfort, but not as sharp. The nausea is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-07-05 08:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re going to clamp your G-tube today and see how you tolerate it. If all goes well, we’ll start a very light diet—bariatric stage 4—later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-07-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s in stage 4? I don’t want to set myself back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-07-05 08:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s pureed foods—smooth, no chunks. We’ll start small and watch for cramping or nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We had to stop the diet advancement. You had some cramping after the stage 4 meal, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it came back—mild but uncomfortable. I think my stomach just can’t handle food yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We agree. We’re going back to NPO and keeping the G-tube to gravity. Also, your tube has been leaking—probably due to a small hole. We’ve scheduled an exchange for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a surgery? I’m nervous about another procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not surgery. Interventional radiology will do it under fluoroscopy—using X-ray guidance. You’ll get light sedation. It’s routine and low risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds better. Will I be able to eat after they change it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-07-06 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO overnight after the exchange, then reassess. If all looks good, we’ll try advancing your diet again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-07-08 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you just got back from the G-tube exchange. It went smoothly—new 18 French MIC tube is in place and working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-07-08 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel much—just some pressure. Is it safe to start eating now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-07-08 14:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO tonight as a precaution. Tomorrow, we’ll start with stage 5—almost regular soft foods—and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you tolerated the stage 5 diet well. No pain, no nausea. Your urine output is good, and you’re walking without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. We’ll switch your pain meds to oral—acetaminophen and a small amount of oxycodone if needed. You’ll finish a 10-day course of antibiotics at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to stay on the soft diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue the bariatric stage 5 diet. Avoid tough or fibrous foods. And crush all pills—no tablets whole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other meds—like Zofran and gabapentin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Resume all your home medications unless we told you otherwise. We’re adding docusate for constipation prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the G-tube? How do I care for it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the site clean and dry. Check daily for redness or drainage. The tube can stay clamped unless you're using it for feeds. We’ll follow up with your surgeon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When should I call the doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you develop fever, vomiting, severe pain, dark stools, or signs of dehydration—like dizziness or dry mouth—call us or go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no driving with the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-07-09 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Avoid driving or heavy machinery while on oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re clearing you for discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take ciprofloxacin twice daily and metronidazole three times daily for 10 days. Finish the whole course, even if you feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And follow up with Dr. ___?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, in about a week. They’ll check your G-tube and assess your recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-07-10 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-07-10 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge—any new pain or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-07-10 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still feeling good. Just ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-07-10 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Nurse will go over your meds and instructions one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-07-10 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to leave whenever you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-07-10 12:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again. I’ll follow up and take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-07-10 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Rest, stay hydrated, and we’ll see you in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-07-10 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, one last thing—should I worry about this happening again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-07-10 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The inflammation was likely due to irritation near the surgical site. With the antibiotics and proper diet, it should resolve. But yes, given your history, we’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-07-10 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-07-10 14:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing everything right. Just keep following the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2174-07-10 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I packed up. Just waiting on the discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2174-07-10 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re ready. I’ll sign off now. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2174-07-10 15:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2174-07-10 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2174-07-10 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, my ride’s here. Can I go now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2174-07-10 16:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re officially discharged. Follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2174-07-10 16:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you!"
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-07-03 21:59:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-07-10 17:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with a two-day history of worsening epigastric and mid-abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting, following a recent gastric bypass reversal. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, IV fluids, and IV pain control. A CT scan revealed significant inflammatory changes near the gastrogastric anastomosis, prompting initiation of ciprofloxacin and metronidazole. Her G-tube was initially placed to gravity drainage for symptom relief. Due to a malfunctioning and leaking G-tube, she underwent a successful exchange to a new 18 French MIC tube under fluoroscopic guidance. After the exchange, she tolerated advancement to a bariatric stage 5 diet, with marked improvement in pain and nausea. She was transitioned to oral pain medications, remained afebrile and hemodynamically stable, and was discharged home on a 10-day course of antibiotics with follow-up instructions. Her mental status remained clear, and she was ambulating independently at discharge.",
    "problems": [
      "Right upper quadrant pain",
      "Gastrostomy malfunction",
      "Nausea",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Polycystic ovarian syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
